ARCHITECTURE (mirrors the A7 DrivesList / TripList precedents)
  VehicleListPageModel.kt      framework-free: VehicleListPageRegistration (vehicles / /vehicles / SLUG /
                               COMPARE_MIN_VEHICLES=2 / COMPARE_PATH / DETAIL_PATH_PREFIX); batterySeverity
                               (web batteryColor: >60 good / >25 warn / else bad -> BatterySeverity enum);
                               deriveVehicleStatus + statusBadge (verbatim web deriveVehicleStatus /
                               statusVariant over VEHICLE_STATES = online/driving/charging/parked/updating/
                               asleep/offline); VehicleListDisplayPrefs (web useUnits — distance unit +
                               convertDistanceFromSI/formatDistance + fmtNumber precision/locale);
                               deriveVehicleListData (the SI->display fold of the four summary metrics, the
                               per-vehicle battery bars, and every vehicle-card value, incl. the pinned-first
                               sortByPins comparator).
  VehicleListPageSource.kt     seam over VehiclesStore.vehicles() (web useVehicles -> GET /vehicles),
                               VehiclesStore.vehicleState(id) (web fetchVehicleState -> GET /vehicles/{id}/state),
                               PinnedStore.pinned(Vehicle) (web usePinned('vehicle') -> GET /pinned?type=vehicle),
                               SettingsStore.settings (web useUnits source), and the syncVehicles / deleteVehicle /
                               togglePin mutations.
  VehicleListPageViewModel.kt  BaseFeedViewModel; vehiclesState: StateFlow<UiState<List<Vehicle>>> over
                               source.vehicles().asUiState (drives loading/empty/error/content); fleetStates:
                               StateFlow<Map<Long,VehicleState?>> = the id-set ▸ flatMapLatest ▸ combine of the
                               per-vehicle fetchVehicleState feeds (web Promise.all); pins + displayPrefs
                               StateFlows; sync / requestDelete / confirmDelete / cancelDelete / togglePin /
                               retry / recordViewOpened; emits the four web toast outcomes through the UiEvent
                               channel.
  VehicleListPage.kt           stateful entry + stateless content; loading skeleton / empty / error-retry /
                               success; the sync success+error banners; the four summary MetricCards in a 2x2
                               grid; the fleet-battery-status GlassPanel of per-vehicle bars; the pinned-sorted
                               vehicle-card list; the remove-confirm dialog; the four toast outcomes via
                               android.widget.Toast (web toast.*). SI converted only at the display boundary;
                               Compose-native (no webview); navigation via the sanctioned deep-link Intent seam.
  VehicleListPageHost.kt       VehicleListRoute() + VehicleListPageHost.register() for the `vehicles` / /vehicles
                               destination (Destinations.kt L52; registered in TeslaSyncApplication.kt).

DATA SOURCES (bound through the ViewModel's StateFlow over the KMP core, P1/S8)
  fetchVehicleState → VehicleListPageSource.fetchVehicleState(id) → VehiclesStore.vehicleState(id)
                      (GET /vehicles/{id}/state) ▸ VehicleListPageViewModel.combineVehicleStates → fleetStates
  usePinned         → VehicleListPageSource.usePinned() → PinnedStore.pinned(PinnedItemType.Vehicle)
                      (GET /pinned?type=vehicle) ▸ VehicleListPageViewModel.pins
  (web useVehicles) → VehicleListPageSource.vehicles() → VehiclesStore.vehicles() (GET /vehicles) ▸ vehiclesState
  (web useUnits)    → VehicleListPageSource.settings() → SettingsStore.settings() ▸ displayPrefs
  The web hook names fetchVehicleState + usePinned are kept verbatim as the Kotlin call-site names (Source +
  ViewModel), so the parity mapping is explicit.

SI BOUNDARY (P1/S5)
  The model stays SI end to end (meters). Display conversion happens only at the render boundary via
  VehicleListDisplayPrefs (convertDistanceFromSI + the shared formatDistance) and the ChartFormat-backed
  fmtNumber. The cache stays SI (ADR-013); no non-SI value is stored or computed. Battery level is a
  dimensionless percent; the "kW" / "%" symbols are unit symbols the web interpolates verbatim (no i18n key on
  the web or in the required string set), reproduced as named constants.

