STRING CATALOG
  23 of the 24 keys already existed in res/values/strings.xml (translation_common_delete / translation_common_noData
  / translation_nav_vehicles + the 20 translation_vehicles_* keys, generated from the shared i18n catalog with the
  verbatim web inline-default values). One key — translation_vehicles_emptyMessage — was absent (the web only carries
  it as the inline `t('vehicles.emptyMessage', 'Connect your Tesla account …')` default), so it was added to
  res/values/strings.xml (an allowed file; sorted before translation_vehicles_emptyTitle) with the verbatim web
  default. The default `values/` catalog is the only string source touched: the build runs no i18n generation, and
  MissingTranslation/ExtraTranslation are disabled (app/build.gradle.kts L114) because ar/he ship as full English
  fallback, so the ar/he mirrors are not required. The status token ({status} badge), the "kW"/"%" unit symbols,
  and the model/VIN subtitle are data-derived values the web likewise renders verbatim (no i18n key on the web or
  in the required string set). The web toast outcomes (syncToast / syncFailed / deleteSuccess / deleteFailed) are
  surfaced as android.widget.Toast via the UiEvent channel — the four messages are pre-resolved with stringResource
  (VehicleListPage.kt L182-185) and shown by Toast.makeText (L199) keyed on the event's i18n key — the native
  analogue of the web `toast.success/error`, so all four strings render from strings.xml.

A11Y / THEME / UNITS (ADR-015)
  - Each battery-bar row carries a merged TalkBack content description ("<name>: <level>%, <range>") via
    Modifier.semantics (BatteryBarRow L541); the lock / sentry / open-detail / remove glyphs carry localized
    content descriptions (translation_common_locked / _sentry / _open / _delete); the decorative metric/header
    icons pass contentDescription=null so accessibility services skip them.
  - Colours/typography come from MaterialTheme + the generated design tokens (TeslaTokens.status.success/warning/
    danger/info for battery severity + sync banners) — dark + dynamic colour honoured; the only fixed colours are
    the per-card MetricCard accents (web color="cyan|green|purple") and the decorative card top-accent gradient
    (web from-cyan via-purple to-green), dynamic gradient stops not static theme tokens, matching the sibling
    DrivesList trend-palette precedent.
  - The summary grid is a responsive 2x2 (web grid-cols-1/2/4). Touch targets use the shared component sizing
    (Button / PinButton). SI values convert only at the display boundary (VehicleListDisplayPrefs); the page is
    Compose-native (no webview). The web page has no chart and no map (0 charts, 0 maps).

NAVIGATION
  No LocalNavController is exposed to page hosts (the ArchivedPage / GlancePage / Settings precedent). The vehicle
  card title + the open-detail button navigate to /vehicles/{id}, and the compare button (shown at >= 2 vehicles)
  to /vehicle-comparison?leftId=&rightId= (web pre-fill), through the sanctioned `teslasync://app/...` deep-link
  ACTION_VIEW Intent seam (openRoute, VehicleListPage.kt L765; NotificationRouteMap.deepLinkUriFor). Not a stub.

